  "description": "<p><strong>Tickets for&nbsp;Old Royal Naval College: Home of The Painted Hall in London</strong><br>\n🎫 Onsite tickets are now discounted for students, jobseekers, and National Art Pass holders.<br>\n🎫 Free entrance is allowed for one under-17 per paying adult and carers of disabled visitors.<br>\n🎫 A multimedia audio guide is provided for the Painted Hall in various languages including English, French, Spanish, Italian, Mandarin, German, and Japanese.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Highlights</strong><br>\n🎨 Be amazed by the impressive Painted Hall in the Old Royal Naval College of Greenwich<br>\n🔊 Utilize an engaging audio guide to discover the story behind Sir James Thornhill's extraordinary artwork and encounter its mythical figures and legendary characters<br>\n🔎 Explore the treasure chest of the Hall to hold the shattered sword of King Louis XIV and don the majestic cloak of King William</p>\n\n<p><strong>General Information</strong><br>\n📅 Date and time:<br>\n- The Painted Hall is available for visitation every day starting at 10 a.m. and closing at 4.30 pm.<br>\n- A talk about The Painted Hall takes place every 30 minutes between 11 am and 4 pm.<br>\n- Guided tours of the site depart from the Visitor Centre every hour between 11 am and 3 pm. If it is available, the Victorian Skittle Alley can be accessed from 12 p.m. to 3 p.m.<br>\n📍 Location: Old Royal Naval College<br>\n⏳ Duration: the length of the daily public guided tours is not specified<br>\n❗ Please note, The Painted Hall closes early or completely on the following days: Wednesday 2 August – early closure, 3 pm, Thursday 16 November – all day, Saturday 2 December – early closure, 3.30 pm, Sunday 24 December – closed all day, Monday 25th December – closed all day and Tuesday 26th December – closed all-day<br>\n♿ Accessibility: the venue is easily accessible for PRM and wheelchair users<br>\n📲 Please check your instructions email for more details</p>\n\n<p><strong>Description</strong><br>\nEmbark on a thrilling adventure at the extraordinary Old Royal Naval College, where British royalty's captivating history comes alive! Get ready to be captivated by the awe-inspiring Painted Hall, an absolute gem reminiscent of the majestic Sistine Chapel. Prepare to be amazed by the wonders of Sir Christopher Wren's architectural genius as you take in jaw-dropping tales woven into the grand ceiling of this extraordinary building. Immerse yourself fully in the experience as you engage with astounding replica artifacts, don King William's legendary cloak, and even challenge Medusa to an epic staring match! Calling all history buffs and film enthusiasts; this spectacular attraction is an absolute must-visit that promises non-stop fun for all! Get your tickets now for the&nbsp;Old Royal Naval College: Home of The Painted Hall in London!</p>",
